# NLSY79 extract - Black-vs-reference educational-attainment gap by family SES level

Script: `analysis/nls_ses_gap.py`  Full log: `outputs/run_log.txt` (== `outputs/stdout.txt`)

## Design actually executed (as pre-registered)

* PRIMARY outcome P3 = highest grade completed (1979) >= 12 among respondents aged >= 20 in 1979 (n=3,487; ages 20-22 so completion is largely settled).
* SECONDARY P1 = grade >= 13 (any post-secondary), P2 = ever DORM/FRATERNITY/SORORITY residence 1981-96.
* APPENDIX = grade >= 16 ('BA-or-higher grade'), descriptive only - see warning below.
* Reference group = NON-BLACK NON-HISPANIC (cohort 3, n=7,510); focal = BLACK (cohort 1, n=2,002); HISPANIC shown descriptively.
* SES index (background, pre-dates outcome): mean of z[max(mother,father) grade], z[occupation prestige rank], z[log family income 1979]; >=2 of 3 items; pooled-sample cuts.
  Occupation is coded by MAJOR GROUP prestige rank validated against independent background markers (rank 1 = labourers 8xx ... rank 10 = professional 0xx).
  Sensitivities: continuous -code occupation, complete-case, occupation dropped, single-proxy indices, endogenous 1985-96 wealth/income/savings.
* GRANULARITY RULE OUTCOME: tertiles FAILED the pre-registered n>=100 rule Black tertile cells 257/108/86 - the high cell has n=86, so the design collapsed to TWO levels at the pooled median, as pre-specified. Final cells (primary outcome): BLACK 303/148, HISPANIC 479/239, NBNH 905/1,413. No cell < 50 (smallest = 148).

