**Warning (binding):** true BA completion is UNOBSERVED in this extract - education is measured only in 1979 when respondents were 14-22 (74.4% of Black respondents were <20). File-wide there are only 37 grade>=16 observations, 5 of them Black, and every Black cell has <10 events; all Fisher exact p > 0.5. These numbers cannot support any statement about a Black advantage or deficit in BA completion, and every respondent achieving grade>=16 was 19-22, i.e. an unusually early/accelerated path rather than a representative one.

## Ability control (attenuation check, not mediation)

* ASVAB columns are mislabelled 'Z Score' in the dictionary (raw column-mean ~460, sd ~90); standardised in-script.
* Adding mean ASVAB Z (same subsample n=2,914): BLACK main OR at low SES 0.423 -> 1.105; interaction OR 2.23 -> 1.92; ASVAB itself LR chi2 = 522.4, p < 1e-100. The low-SES deficit is largely, though not entirely, accounted for by measured baseline preparedness.